fix: v1.3.1 - convert installer to CommonJS for npm postinstall reliability

The v1.3.0 installer used ESM (install.mjs). On Windows with Node 24 and
npm 11, the global install pipeline misreports the postinstall script
path for .mjs files, surfacing a phantom MODULE_NOT_FOUND exit-1 even
when the script ran successfully and SKILL.md was copied into place.

CommonJS (install.cjs) is the lifecycle convention used by mature
packages such as the official Claude Code package (which uses
install.cjs and exits cleanly). Switching to CJS avoids the issue.

Files changed:
- install.cjs: new CommonJS installer (functional equivalent of the
  former install.mjs).
- install.mjs: removed.
- package.json: removed "type": "module"; main, postinstall, test, and
  files array now reference install.cjs.
- CHANGELOG.md: v1.3.1 entry covers the fix.

No skill behavior change. SKILL.md content is byte-identical to v1.3.0.

Author: Orlando Molina - TruePointAgents

